    "name": "native-agent-surface",
    "description": "Discover and use the host software an agent runs in or through — local session transports (cmux), terminal multiplexers (tmux, zellij), and other agentic shells/harnesses — via a capability-first, host-neutral adapter contract. Use when an agent needs to detect which native surfaces are present, route on declared capabilities instead of hard-coding one tool, reuse a project workspace before creating one, bootstrap a project, run browser E2E, or coordinate bounded multi-model sessions without serializing environment values or socket capabilities. cmux is the first adapter, not the universal surface.",
